WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.810
Game of Thrones has been all about big revelations
lately.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.130
Beyond the explicit discoveries made by fans
and characters in the show's last few episodes,

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.449
however, the show may also have inadvertently
revealed something else about its primary

00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:13.449
villain.

00:00:13.449 --> 00:00:17.130
One fan theory currently taking the internet
by storm claims that Thrones may have already

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.520
spoiled the identity of the Night King.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.500
Though this theory has circulated through
the web since season seven concluded, it found

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.580
new traction following HBO's Inside the Episode
featurette for the season 8 premiere.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.850
During the post-episode promo, Thrones co-showrunner
and director David Benioff offered up information

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:38.510
that many are taking as evidence that the
Night King is, in fact, a secret Targaryen.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.140
"No one has ever ridden a dragon [...] except
for Dany.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.800
Only Targaryens can ride dragons, and that
should be a sign for Jon.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.170
Jon's not always the quickest on the uptick
but eventually gets there."

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:53.500
As the son of Rhaegar Targaryen and Lyanna
Stark, Jon's Targaryen blood makes him worthy

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.469
to ride a dragon, though he doesn't know it
at the time.

00:00:56.469 --> 00:01:00.570
And while Benioff might be right in saying
that only Targaryens can ride dragons, he's

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.110
wrong to say that Dany was the only person
to have ridden a dragon before the first episode

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.230
of season 8.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.230
Remember this?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.040
(why you shouldn't you mix Pop Rocks and Slurpees)

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.940
That makes three people who have ridden dragons
during the series so far: Daenerys on Drogon,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.220
Jon on Rhaegal, and the Night King on Viserion.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.550
Naturally, this has a huge subsection of the
Game of Thrones fandom thinking the Night

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.480
King could be a Targaryen.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.441
After all, if dragon riders are Targaryens
and the Night King is a dragon rider, then

00:01:30.441 --> 00:01:34.020
surely the Night King must be a Targaryen,
too?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.780
Unfortunately, it's not hard to pick holes
in this theory.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.210
For starters, Viserion isn't the same type
of dragon he was before he died.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:45.470
He's an Ice Dragon now, not a Fire Dragon,
and it stands to reason that the old rules

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.110
don't exactly apply in this situation.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:52.140
And while the Targaryens do have a deep connection
with dragons, they don't appear to have any

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.220
historic link to Ice Dragons.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.720
According to Game of Thrones author George
R.R. Martin's novella The Ice Dragon, humans

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.550
can't tame, train, or ride Ice Dragons.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.920
A portion of the text reads:

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.400
"We have tales of those that tried, found
frozen with their whip and harness in hand.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:11.110
I've heard about people that have lost hands
or fingers just by touching one of them.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.110
Frostbite."

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.770
Another problem with the theory that the Night
King is a Targaryen is that the Night King

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:21.010
is a member of the First Men, who came to
Westeros from Essos 12,000 years prior to

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.600
the Targaryen Conquest.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:27.231
After the First Men invaded Westeros, the
ancient Westerosi inhabitants known as the

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:31.130
Children of the Forest captured one of them
- and the Night King was born.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:36.380
Neither House Targaryen nor the Valyrian Empire
from which they came were around during this

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.650
time, and the Targaryens didn't rise to power
in the Valyrian Freehold until thousands of

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.710
years after the war between the First Men
and the Children of the Forest.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:48.580
Taking this timeline into account, it seems
impossible that the First Man who became the

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.880
Night King could have been a Targaryen.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.650
On the other hand, there's no getting around
one strange similarity between the Night King

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.050
and House Targaryen that people picked up
on during the season 8 premiere.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:03.510
In one of the final scenes of the episode,
Eddison Tollet, Beric Dondarrion, and others

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:08.140
reach Last Hearth and find little Lord Umber
pinned to a wall with several severed limbs

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:11.130
surrounding his body, mapped out in the shape
of a spiral.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:15.480
We've seen that spiral a few times before:
once around the Weirwood tree when the Children

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.209
of the Forest created the Night King, again
when the White Walkers slaughtered horses

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:24.060
to terrorize the wildlings, and finally in
etchings carved in the caves of Dragonstone.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.060
But it might not be a coincidence that this
spiral also looks a whole lot like the sigil

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.040
of House Targaryen - and spirals of a kind
have even been known to appear around the

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.240
story's two living Targaryens.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.940
Could this mean that the Night King is related
to the Targaryen family in some way?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.610
Considering his ability to ride Viserion,
there really may be some relation.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.730
Then again, maybe there isn't.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.290
"Close the bloody gate."

